package lagrange:assets@0.1.0;

/// The host provides durable asset bytes to the renderer Component at runtime.
/// The renderer requests an asset by name; the host returns its bytes or an
/// error. This is the asset-transfer seam: upstream wasi-gfx examples bake
/// assets in at build time (include_bytes!); Lagrange loads them at runtime so
/// a GLB chosen at Session time can reach the running Component.
///
/// Ownership: the host realization is BrowserRendererAdapter host wiring
/// (src/browser-renderer/assets.js `createAssetProvider`) — an injected,
/// attach-scoped byte source bound into ONE Component instance's import closure
/// (jco instantiation mode), NOT an asset store and NOT a process-global. The
/// asset-bytes authority (resolving durable refs to bytes under object/read) is
/// the environment's authorized read lane (`ImageClientAdapter.resolveAssetBytes`);
/// the adapter receives only the opaque attach-scoped allowlist. (Resolved by
/// Bead lagrange-object-environment-0dm.)
interface provider {
    /// Load an asset's bytes by its PRESENTATION-LOCAL name. The name is an
    /// opaque string scoped to THIS attach's allowlist (e.g. "main-model"); it
    /// is never an image/object id and never another attach's name. Returns
    /// the bytes, or an error string when the name is not in this attach's
    /// allowlist. Format-neutral (the Component interprets the bytes; the host
    /// treats them as opaque).
    load: func(name: string) -> result<list<u8>, string>;
}
